<!DOCTYPE Menu PUBLIC "-//freedesktop//DTD Menu 1.0//EN"
 "http://www.freedesktop.org/standards/menu-spec/menu-1.0.dtd">
<!-- An "Amateur Radio" submenu for every application that says HamRadio.

     KDE, XFCE, MATE and Raspberry Pi OS have no amateur-radio section of
     their own: HamRadio is only an "additional" category in the menu spec,
     so a ham app is filed by whatever main category sits beside it - ours
     said Network and landed under Internet (Brian, 08/10/2026: wanted its
     own submenu). Same-named menus merge, so OpenHamShack QO-100 NB and OpenHamShack Radio
     each ship one of these under its own name and either alone is enough;
     removing one package leaves the other's.

     Every HamRadio app is included, WSJT-X and fldigi too, but only our
     own are taken out of Internet - moving somebody else's app away from
     where its packager put it is not ours to do. GNOME ignores merged
     menus and finds apps by search, which is harmless. -->
<Menu>
  <Name>Applications</Name>
  <Menu>
    <Name>HamRadio</Name>
    <Directory>@PKG@-hamradio.directory</Directory>
    <Include>
      <Category>HamRadio</Category>
    </Include>
  </Menu>
  <Menu>
    <Name>Internet</Name>
    <Exclude>
      <Filename>@PKG@.desktop</Filename>
    </Exclude>
  </Menu>
</Menu>
